---
import LegalLayout from "~/layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "~/lib/site";
const updated = "July 29, 2026";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie Policy — CartConsent"
  description="How this website uses cookies and similar technologies, and how you can control them."
  heading="Cookie Policy"
  updated={updated}
>
  <p>
    This policy explains how <strong>{SITE.name}</strong> uses cookies and similar technologies on
    this website. Cookies are small files stored on your device. We use them to make the site work,
    remember your preferences, and — with your consent — to measure traffic and support marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>Categories we use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Essential</strong> — required for the site to function and to remember your consent choices. Always on.</li>
    <li><strong>Preferences</strong> — remember choices like layout and region.</li>
    <li><strong>Statistics</strong> — help us understand how the site is used so we can improve it.</li>
    <li><strong>Marketing</strong> — used to measure and, where applicable, personalize advertising.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Managing cookies</h2>
  <p>
    You can change your choices at any time using the consent controls on this site, and you can block
    or delete cookies in your browser settings. We honor the Global Privacy Control (GPC) signal where
    the law treats it as a valid opt-out.
  </p>
  <p>
    Non-essential cookies are not set until you consent. If you decline, only the essential cookies
    needed to run the site and remember that choice are used.
  </p>

  <h2>Practicing what we preach</h2>
  <div class="note">
    This site runs the same consent-first approach our plugin gives your store: non-essential trackers
    stay blocked until you choose, GPC is honored, and your choice is respected. Reopen your
    preferences any time from the link in the footer.
  </div>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about cookies on this site? Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
